      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen, which is twice the usual maximum daily dose for adults. That maximum is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nMaybe the intended dose was different. Common regimens include:\n- 400\u2013800 mg by mouth three or four times daily, not to exceed 3,200 mg/day\n- 1,600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily\n\nAlso, orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. If you're relaying this for a clinician, please have them confirm the intended dose and frequency, or enter the order themselves.\n\nIf you send me a corrected dose, or confirmation from the prescriber, I can enter it right away."
      }
